; lib/js_ast, rebuilt for Melange. Same copy-never-fork rule as the core and
; walk_core mirrors: anything that changes in lib/js_ast changes here on the next
; build, so the Melange run cannot silently test older code than the native
; golden.
;
; The printer is the reason to mirror it. Its [Number] literals go through
; [Printf "%.17g"] and its [Bigint] literals through [Int64.to_string], which
; Melange implements itself (its own float formatter, and Int64 as a pair of
; 32-bit words) rather than sharing jsoo's or glibc's. The probe's js_ast section
; diffs the printed text of a fixed corpus across all three backends.
;
; jsoo needs no mirror: js_ast reaches no Expr.

(copy_files
 (files %{workspace_root}/lib/js_ast/*.{ml,mli}))

(library
 (name js_ast_mel)
 (wrapped false)
 (modes melange)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{profile} melange))
 (libraries fmt_mel))
